---
// Signatures: timing that belongs to the thing itself, which no term carries
// (docs/motion.md, Signatures). Each is declared where it is defined, with its
// reason and its form with less motion.
import edgeSource from "@kinra/web/registry/patterns/live-edge/live-edge.html?raw";

const edge = (state: string, title: string, meta: string) =>
	edgeSource
		.replace(
			'data-edge="working"',
			`data-edge="ready" data-lab-edge-state="${state}"`,
		)
		.replace("Indexing files", title)
		.replace(
			'<p class="kin-list__meta">Working</p>',
			`<p class="kin-list__meta">${meta}</p>`,
		);

const ops = [
	[12, 70],
	[40, 22],
	[78, 58],
	[110, 18],
	[146, 64],
	[176, 30],
	[204, 66],
	[232, 24],
];
const path = ops
	.map(([x, y], index) => `${index ? "L" : "M"}${x} ${y}`)
	.join(" ");
---

<article class="lab-specimen" id="X1" data-lab-signature="edge">
	<div class="lab-specimen__head">
		<span class="lab-id">X1</span>
		<h3 class="lab-term">The live edge</h3>
		<div class="lab-actions">
			<button
				class="kin-button"
				data-size="compact"
				type="button"
				data-lab-run
				aria-pressed="false"
			>
				Show the states
			</button>
		</div>
		<p class="lab-meaning">
			A stable pattern's own timings: the working band (2.4s), the breath while
			the next move is the person's (3.2s), the blink while reconnecting (1.2s)
			and the gather that ends work (1.1s, as long as the closing state).
		</p>
		<p class="lab-note">
			Open for review: "nothing blinks" asks whether waiting and reconnecting
			should hold still. Each is shown as it is today and as a still line beside
			it. Changing a stable pattern's form needs a migration note.
		</p>
	</div>
	<div class="lab-pair">
		<div>
			<p class="lab-pair__label">Today, as signatures</p>
			<ul class="lab-edge-row lab-edge-list">
				<Fragment
					set:html={edge("working", "Indexing files", "Working · band 2.4s")}
				/>
				<Fragment
					set:html={edge("waiting", "Your answer", "Waiting · breath 3.2s")}
				/>
				<Fragment
					set:html={edge(
						"reconnecting",
						"The connection",
						"Reconnecting · blink 1.2s",
					)}
				/>
			</ul>
		</div>
		<div>
			<p class="lab-pair__label">The still alternative</p>
			<ul class="lab-edge-row lab-edge-list lab-edge-still">
				<Fragment
					set:html={edge("working", "Indexing files", "Working · band 2.4s")}
				/>
				<Fragment
					set:html={edge("waiting", "Your answer", "Waiting · a steady line")}
				/>
				<Fragment
					set:html={edge(
						"reconnecting",
						"The connection",
						"Reconnecting · still dashes",
					)}
				/>
			</ul>
		</div>
	</div>
</article>

<article class="lab-specimen" id="X2" data-lab-signature="escapement">
	<div class="lab-specimen__head">
		<span class="lab-id">X2</span>
		<h3 class="lab-term">The escapement</h3>
		<div class="lab-actions">
			<button
				class="kin-button"
				data-size="compact"
				type="button"
				data-lab-run
				aria-pressed="false"
			>
				Start the clock
			</button>
			<button
				class="kin-button"
				data-size="compact"
				type="button"
				data-lab-gait
				aria-pressed="true"
			>
				Locked to the pulse
			</button>
		</div>
		<p class="lab-meaning">
			Observatory's seconds hand beats dead seconds while it is locked to the
			GPS pulse: each second it swings to the mark and 0.6° past it in 60ms,
			falls back in 40ms and holds. Coasting, it sweeps, and the dial says why.
			Its timing is the escapement's own gait, so it is a signature, not a
			settle.
		</p>
		<p class="lab-note">
			Rebuilt from Observatory's <code>movement.ts</code>: one minute-long
			animation of 181 keyframes, started from the clock. A change of gait waits
			until just after a second and keeps the phase. With less motion it steps
			once a second.
		</p>
	</div>
	<div class="lab-columns">
		<div class="lab-col" data-kin-motion="expressive">
			<div class="lab-stage">
				<div class="x2-dial" aria-hidden="true">
					<span class="x2-hand" data-x2-hand></span>
				</div>
				<p class="lab-caption" data-x2-caption>Stopped.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</article>

<article class="lab-specimen" id="X3" data-lab-signature="playback">
	<div class="lab-specimen__head">
		<span class="lab-id">X3</span>
		<h3 class="lab-term">Playback</h3>
		<div class="lab-actions">
			<button
				class="kin-button"
				data-size="compact"
				type="button"
				data-lab-play
				aria-pressed="false"
			>
				Play
			</button>
		</div>
		<p class="lab-meaning">
			Relay's Play runs a program's path in about half a minute however long the
			machine takes. Nothing moves until Play is pressed; it stops at the end,
			on Pause, off screen and in a hidden tab, and no frame is drawn after it
			stops. With less motion it goes an operation at a time.
		</p>
		<p class="lab-note">
			Relay decision 0070: ten to forty seconds, six plus three a span; with
			less motion the first operation after 600ms and each next after 900ms.
		</p>
	</div>
	<div class="lab-columns">
		<div class="lab-col" data-kin-motion="productive">
			<svg class="x3-path" viewBox="0 0 244 84" aria-hidden="true">
				<path class="x3-route" d={path}></path>
				{ops.map(([x, y]) => <circle class="x3-op" cx={x} cy={y} r="2.4" />)}
				<circle class="x3-tool" data-x3-tool cx={ops[0][0]} cy={ops[0][1]} r="4"
				></circle>
			</svg>
			<p class="lab-caption" data-x3-caption>Operation 1 of {ops.length}</p>
			<p class="lab-check" data-lab-check>
				Nothing moves until Play is pressed.
			</p>
			<script
				is:inline
				type="application/json"
				data-x3-ops
				set:html={JSON.stringify(ops)}
			/>
		</div>
	</div>
</article>
